        textProvided: "Of the host whom I NAMED<br>As friends, ye alone<br>Dear few!, were ashamed<br>In troubles unknown<br>To leave me deserted; but boldly ye cherished my cause as your own.<br>My thanks shall endure<br>– The poor tribute I paid<br>To a faith that was pure –<br>Till my ashes be laid<br>In the urn; and the Stygian boatman I seek, an impalpable shade.<br>But nay! For the days<br>Of a mortal are few;<br>Shall they limit your praise<br>Nay rather to you<br>Each new generation shall offer – if aught be remembered – your due.<br>For the lofty frame<br>That my VERSES ENFOLD,<br>Men still shall acclaim<br>Thro’ ages untold:<br>And still shall they speak of your virtue; your honour they still shall uphold.",
